# Korean Localization Guidelines

## Language & Text

- All user-facing text should be in Korean
- Use formal/polite Korean (존댓말) for game instructions and UI
- Puzzle content can use casual Korean (반말) for character dialogue
- Maintain consistent terminology across all game elements

## Typography & Fonts

- Primary font: Gaegu (Google Fonts) as defined in [src/app/layout.tsx](mdc:src/app/layout.tsx)
- Font weights: 300 (light), 400 (regular), 700 (bold)
- Ensure proper Korean character rendering and spacing

## Content Guidelines

- Puzzle questions should be clear and unambiguous in Korean
- Hints should provide helpful guidance without giving away answers
- Error messages and feedback should be user-friendly in Korean
- Room titles should be engaging and descriptive

## Cultural Considerations

- Use Korean cultural references appropriately in puzzles
- Consider Korean educational standards for difficulty levels
- Ensure content is appropriate for the target age group (elementary school level)

## Technical Implementation

- HTML lang attribute set to "ko" in root layout
- Use proper Korean text encoding (UTF-8)
- Consider Korean text length in UI design (Korean text can be longer than English)
- Test Korean text rendering across different devices and browsers
